        body: {
            data: {
                html: '<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" lang="en" style="height: 100%;">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset="UTF-8">\n    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">\n    <meta name="csrf-token" content>\n    \n  <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="https://assets.mlcdn.com/fonts-v2.css?version=1793185736952">\n<style type="text/css">\n* { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }\n\n        img { outline: none; text-decoration: none; display: block; }\n        a img { border: none; }\n\n        a[href^=&quot;tel&quot;], a[href^=&quot;sms&quot;] { text-decoration: none; pointer-events: none; cursor: default; }\n@import url(https://assets.mlcdn.com/fonts-v2.css?version=1793185736952);\n\n\n        @media (max-width: 767px) {\n            #ml-preview-wrapper.ml-site h1.ml-content-heading { font-size: 24px; }\n            #ml-preview-wrapper.ml-site h2.ml-content-heading { font-size: 24px; }\n            #ml-preview-wrapper.ml-site h3.ml-content-heading { font-size: 20px; }\n            #ml-preview-wrapper.ml-site h4.ml-content-heading { font-size: 18px; }\n            #ml-preview-wrapper.ml-site p.ml-p-1 { font-size: 16px; }\n            #ml-preview-wrapper.ml-site p.ml-p-2 { font-size: 14px; }\n            #ml-preview-wrapper.ml-site p.ml-p-3 { font-size: 12px; }\n        }\n</style>\n</head>\n  <body style="min-height: 100%; margin: 0; background-color: #ffffff;">\n    <div id="app" style="height: 100%;"><div class="ml-nbx" data-version="2.82.1" style="height: 100%;"><!----><!----><table id="ml-preview-wrapper" class="ml-email ml-site" width="100%" role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" bgcolor="#ffffff" style="font-family: \'DM Sans\', sans-serif, \'Arial\', \'Helvetica\', sans-serif; color: #333333; font-size: 16px; background-color: #ffffff;"><tbody><tr><td align="center" valign="top"><!--[--><!--]--><!--[--><!--]--><table width="100%" style="max-width:640px;" role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" align="center"><tbody><tr><td class="py-6 px-4" style="padding-left: 16px; padding-right: 16px; padding-top: 24px; padding-bottom: 24px;"><!--[--><!--[--><table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" class="ml-email-text-table ml-inline-email-node w-full" style="width: 100%;"><tbody><tr><td dir="ltr" style="padding-top: 12px;"><h1 dir="ltr" class="ml-content-heading" style="font-family: \'Merriweather\', serif, \'Arial\', \'Helvetica\', sans-serif; font-weight: 700; line-height: 150%; letter-spacing: 0px; color: #111111; font-size: 32px; margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: left;">The Everly Brief</h1></td></tr></tbody></table><!--]--><!--[--><table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" class="ml-email-text-table ml-inline-email-node w-full" style="width: 100%;"><tbody><tr><td dir="ltr" style="padding-top: 12px;"><p dir="ltr" class="ml-p ml-p-1" style="margin-top: 0; font-family: \'DM Sans\', sans-serif, \'Arial\', \'Helvetica\', sans-serif; font-weight: 400; line-height: 150%; letter-spacing: 0px; font-size: 16px; color: #333333; margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: left;">This week I went deep on one question: why do some tiny newsletters feel more alive than publications with full editorial teams? I think I found the answer — and it\'s not what I expected.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><!--]--><!--[--><table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" class="ml-email-image-table ml-inline-email-node w-full" style="width: 100%;"><tbody><tr><td align="center" dir="ltr" style="padding-top: 12px;"><!--[if mso]><img src="https://assets.mlcdn.com/images/v2/templates/40/40003/the-everly-brief.jpg" alt="" width="640" height="427" style="display:block;" /><![endif]--><!--[if !mso]><!--><img src="https://assets.mlcdn.com/images/v2/templates/40/40003/the-everly-brief.jpg" alt width="100%" style="display:block;width:100%;max-width:640px;height:auto;"><!--<![endif]--><p dir="ltr" class="node-image-caption ml-p ml-p-1" style="margin-top: 0; font-family: \'DM Sans\', sans-serif, \'Arial\', \'Helvetica\', sans-serif; font-weight: 400; line-height: 150%; letter-spacing: 0px; font-size: 16px; color: #333333; margin-bottom: 4px; margin: 4px 0 0; text-align: center;">A quiet desk, a blank page, and the question every writer eventually asks: who am I actually writing this for?</p></td></tr></tbody></table><!--]--><!--[--><table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" class="ml-email-text-table ml-inline-email-node w-full" style="width: 100%;"><tbody><tr><td dir="ltr" style="padding-top: 12px;"><h2 dir="ltr" class="ml-content-heading" style="font-family: \'Merriweather\', serif, \'Arial\', \'Helvetica\', sans-serif; font-weight: 700; line-height: 150%; letter-spacing: 0px; color: #111111; font-size: 24px; margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: left;">The Deep Dive</h2></td></tr></tbody></table><!--]--><!--[--><table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" class="ml-email-text-table ml-inline-email-node w-full" style="width: 100%;"><tbody><tr><td dir="ltr" style="padding-top: 12px;"><p dir="ltr" class="ml-p ml-p-1" style="margin-top: 0; font-family: \'DM Sans\', sans-serif, \'Arial\', \'Helvetica\', sans-serif; font-weight: 400; line-height: 150%; letter-spacing: 0px; font-size: 16px; color: #333333; margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: left;">Most advice about newsletter writing focuses on tactics — subject lines, send times, content length. But the writers with the most loyal audiences tend to share one quiet habit that has nothing to do with any of that.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><!--]--><!--[--><table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" class="ml-email-text-table ml-inline-email-node w-full" style="width: 100%;"><tbody><tr><td dir="ltr" style="padding-top: 12px;"><h3 dir="ltr" class="ml-content-heading" style="font-family: \'Merriweather\', serif, \'Arial\', \'Helvetica\', sans-serif; font-weight: 700; line-height: 150%; letter-spacing: 0px; color: #111111; font-size: 20px; margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: left;">The quiet advantage of writing to one person</h3></td></tr></tbody></table><!--]--><!--[--><table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" class="ml-email-text-table ml-inline-email-node w-full" style="width: 100%;"><tbody><tr><td dir="ltr" style="padding-top: 12px;"><p dir="ltr" class="ml-p ml-p-1" style="margin-top: 0; font-family: \'DM Sans\', sans-serif, \'Arial\', \'Helvetica\', sans-serif; font-weight: 400; line-height: 150%; letter-spacing: 0px; font-size: 16px; color: #333333; margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: left;">The best newsletters don\'t feel like broadcasts. They feel like a message from a friend who happens to know a lot. This piece breaks down the specific writing habits that create that intimacy — and how to build them into your own process.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><!--]--><!--[--><table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" class="w-full ml-email-divider-table ml-inline-email-node" style="width: 100%;"><tbody><tr><td align="center" style="padding-top: 12px;"><table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%"><tbody><tr><td height="1" style="padding-top: 12px; border-top: 1px solid #e5e5e5; line-height: 0; font-size: 0;"></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table><!--]--><!--[--><table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" class="ml-email-text-table ml-inline-email-node w-full" style="width: 100%;"><tbody><tr><td dir="ltr" style="padding-top: 12px;"><h2 dir="ltr" class="ml-content-heading" style="font-family: \'Merriweather\', serif, \'Arial\', \'Helvetica\', sans-serif; font-weight: 700; line-height: 150%; letter-spacing: 0px; color: #111111; font-size: 24px; margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: left;">Worth Bookmarking</h2></td></tr></tbody></table><!--]--><!--[--><table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" class="ml-email-text-table ml-inline-email-node w-full" style="width: 100%;"><tbody><tr><td dir="ltr" style="padding-top: 12px;"><p dir="ltr" class="ml-p ml-p-1" style="margin-top: 0; font-family: \'DM Sans\', sans-serif, \'Arial\', \'Helvetica\', sans-serif; font-weight: 400; line-height: 150%; letter-spacing: 0px; font-size: 16px; color: #333333; margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: left;"><strong>The 2-minute inbox audit</strong> — Scan your last 10 emails. Which ones did you open immediately? Which did you skip? The pattern tells you everything about your subject lines.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><!--]--><!--[--><table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" class="ml-email-text-table ml-inline-email-node w-full" style="width: 100%;"><tbody><tr><td dir="ltr" style="padding-top: 12px;"><p dir="ltr" class="ml-p ml-p-1" style="margin-top: 0; font-family: \'DM Sans\', sans-serif, \'Arial\', \'Helvetica\', sans-serif; font-weight: 400; line-height: 150%; letter-spacing: 0px; font-size: 16px; color: #333333; margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: left;"><strong>Why "valuable content" is bad advice</strong> — Everyone says it. Nobody defines it. This essay finally does — and the answer is more specific than you\'d think.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><!--]--><!--[--><table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" class="ml-email-text-table ml-inline-email-node w-full" style="width: 100%;"><tbody><tr><td dir="ltr" style="padding-top: 12px;"><p dir="ltr" class="ml-p ml-p-1" style="margin-top: 0; font-family: \'DM Sans\', sans-serif, \'Arial\', \'Helvetica\', sans-serif; font-weight: 400; line-height: 150%; letter-spacing: 0px; font-size: 16px; color: #333333; margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: left;"><strong>How Lenny Rachitsky built to 700k subscribers</strong> — This is the one I mentioned above. One decision early on changed everything. Worth reading slowly.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><!--]--><!--[--><table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" class="w-full ml-email-divider-table ml-inline-email-node" style="width: 100%;"><tbody><tr><td align="center" style="padding-top: 12px;"><table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%"><tbody><tr><td height="1" style="padding-top: 12px; border-top: 1px solid #e5e5e5; line-height: 0; font-size: 0;"></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table><!--]--><!--[--><table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" class="ml-email-text-table ml-inline-email-node w-full" style="width: 100%;"><tbody><tr><td dir="ltr" style="padding-top: 12px;"><h2 dir="ltr" class="ml-content-heading" style="font-family: \'Merriweather\', serif, \'Arial\', \'Helvetica\', sans-serif; font-weight: 700; line-height: 150%; letter-spacing: 0px; color: #111111; font-size: 24px; margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: left;">Enjoyed this issue?</h2></td></tr></tbody></table><!--]--><!--[--><table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" class="ml-email-text-table ml-inline-email-node w-full" style="width: 100%;"><tbody><tr><td dir="ltr" style="padding-top: 12px;"><p dir="ltr" class="ml-p ml-p-1" style="margin-top: 0; font-family: \'DM Sans\', sans-serif, \'Arial\', \'Helvetica\', sans-serif; font-weight: 400; line-height: 150%; letter-spacing: 0px; font-size: 16px; color: #333333; margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: left;">I have been writing The Everly Brief for three years — every week, no exceptions. No ads, no sponsors, no fluff. Just the most interesting things she found, written the way she\'d explain them to a friend over coffee. If this issue resonated, there are 150 more in the archive — and a new one lands every Tuesday.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><!--]--><!--[--><table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" class="w-full ml-email-button-table ml-inline-email-node" style="width: 100%;"><tbody><tr><td align="center" dir="ltr" style="padding-top: 12px;"><!--[if mso]><v:roundrect xmlns:v="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:vml" xmlns:w="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word" href="#" target="_self" style="width:400px;height:44px;v-text-anchor:middle;" arcsize="16%" stroke="f" strokecolor="#22c55e" strokeweight="0px"><v:fill color="#ef4444" opacity="100%"/><w:anchorlock/><v:textbox inset="0,0,0,0"><center style="padding-top:12px;padding-bottom:12px;padding-left:20px;padding-right:20px;"><span style="font-family: \'DM Sans\', sans-serif;color:#ffffff;font-size:15px;line-height:15px;mso-line-height-rule:exactly;font-weight:600">If you enjoyed this issue, pass it along</span></center></v:textbox></v:roundrect><![endif]--><!--[if !mso]><!--><table class="ml-email-button-table" role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="border-radius:8px;overflow:hidden;"><tr><td style="padding-top: 12px; background-color: #ef4444; padding: 0;" bgcolor="#ef4444"><span style="display:block;background-color:#ef4444;border-radius:8px"><a dir="ltr" href="#" style="color:#ffffff;font-family: \'DM Sans\', sans-serif;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:0.375px;font-size:15px;line-height:1.4;text-decoration:none;text-align:center;display:block;padding:12px 20px;margin:0;background-color:transparent" target="_self" linkid="103">If you enjoyed this issue, pass it along</a></span></td></tr></table><!--<![endif]--></td></tr></tbody></table><!--]--><!--[--><table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" class="w-full ml-email-divider-table ml-inline-email-node" style="width: 100%;"><tbody><tr><td align="center" style="padding-top: 12px;"><table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%"><tbody><tr><td height="1" style="padding-to